.el .ds Aq '
.TH PDFLUENT-XFA-FLATTEN 1  "pdfluent 1.1.0" PDFluent
.SH NAME
pdfluent\-xfa\-flatten \- Flatten an XFA/AcroForm document (not yet implemented in the public CLI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpdfluent xfa flatten\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] <\fB\-o\fR|\fB\-\-out\fR> [\fB\-\-policy\fR] [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-\-experimental\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR]... [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Flatten an XFA/AcroForm document (not yet implemented in the public CLI).
.PP
XFA support is EXPERIMENTAL and feature\-gated — no Adobe Reader parity claim. `\-\-policy saved\-state` (default) honors the document\*(Aqs saved form state; `\-\-policy fresh\-merge` is EXPERIMENTAL, opt\-in, and never the default (requires `\-\-experimental`).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Machine\-readable JSON envelope on stdout
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-out\fR \fI<OUT>\fR
Output PDF file
.TP
\fB\-\-policy\fR \fI<POLICY>\fR [default: saved\-state]
XFA rendering policy: `saved\-state` (default) or `fresh\-merge` (experimental, opt\-in)
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Quiet: human mode prints data only (no warnings or progress notes)
.TP
\fB\-\-experimental\fR
Acknowledge that you are using an experimental, opt\-in code path
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Verbose stderr diagnostics (repeat for more)
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>
Input PDF file
.SH VERSION
v1.1.0
